From 65cb25c9084ed372afa70feb2bcad28bfa3bf34a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baineng Shou <shoubaineng@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:13:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: dw-axi-dmac: report DMA_PAUSED in tx_status

dma_chan_tx_status() never returns DMA_PAUSED even after the client has
paused the channel: dma_cookie_status() can only yield COMPLETE or
IN_PROGRESS, and the previous

    if (chan->is_paused && ret == DMA_IN_PROGRESS)
        ret = DMA_PAUSED;

mapping was dropped when dma_chan_tx_status() was rewritten to add burst
residue reporting in commit 8e55444da65c ("dmaengine: dw-axi-dmac:
Support burst residue granularity"). Restore it so clients that
distinguish a paused transfer from a running one get the correct status.

The check is placed under vc.lock together with the residue calculation,
since is_paused is documented as protected by vc.lock. The residue
itself is unaffected: while paused the hardware is suspended, so
completed_blocks does not advance and the reported residue stays valid.

Fixes: 8e55444da65c ("dmaengine: dw-axi-dmac: Support burst residue granularity")
Signed-off-by: Baineng Shou <shoubaineng@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c b/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c
index bcefaff03b5c..9dc1cf6ce5fe 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c
@@ -372,6 +372,9 @@ dma_chan_tx_status(struct dma_chan *dchan, dma_cookie_t cookie,
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&chan->vc.lock, flags);
 
+	if (chan->is_paused && status == DMA_IN_PROGRESS)
+		status = DMA_PAUSED;
+
 	vdesc = vchan_find_desc(&chan->vc, cookie);
 	if (vdesc) {
 		length = vd_to_axi_desc(vdesc)->length;
-- 
2.34.1

